## Landing page: questions and closing
faq-eyebrow = Questions
faq-title = Good to know.
faq-more = More answers in Help
faq-q-free = Is it really free?
faq-a-free = Yes. Standard voices have no hours limit, and there is no card, trial or ad. Expressive voices run on shared graphics hardware, so each person gets a fair share of minutes every day.
faq-q-voices = Which voices are there?
faq-a-voices = Twenty-eight standard voices in American and British English, five expressive voices, and your own voice once you record it.
faq-q-own-voice = Can it read in my own voice?
faq-a-own-voice = Yes. Read eight short lines aloud in a quiet room and Streams Reader builds your voice from them. Only you can use it.
faq-q-screen-off = Does it keep playing with the screen off?
faq-a-screen-off = Yes, once you install it to your home screen. The native apps will add lock-screen and headset controls.
faq-q-files = What can I import?
faq-a-files = Web articles by link, PDF, EPUB, Markdown and plain text files, and anything you paste.
faq-q-data = Where are my documents kept?
faq-a-data = In your account, on the services listed in our { $privacy } policy. We don’t run ads or trackers, and we don’t sell data.
faq-q-languages = Which languages does it read?
faq-a-languages = The voices read English today. The app itself is in eight languages, and more reading languages are planned.
faq-q-sources = Where do the free books come from?
faq-a-sources = From Standard Ebooks, a volunteer project that publishes carefully edited public-domain books. They are free to read and share in the U.S.; outside the U.S., check your local laws.
faq-q-iphone = Is there an iPhone app?
faq-a-iphone = Not yet. On iPhone and iPad, open Streams Reader in Safari and add it to your Home Screen.
faq-q-extension = Is there a browser extension?
faq-a-extension = It’s on the way. It adds a button that reads the page you’re on aloud in Streams Reader.
