## llms.txt (English only)
llms-summary = Streams Reader is a free, open-source read-aloud app. It reads web articles, PDFs, EPUBs and pasted text aloud in natural voices (Kokoro-82M), expressive voices (Ming-3.0-tts) or the listener’s own cloned voice, highlighting each word as it is spoken. It runs in the browser today; Android, macOS, Windows and Linux apps are in development. A sub-brand of Streams (streams.watch).
llms-home = what Streams Reader is, its voices, platforms and FAQ
llms-download = the web app and the status of the native apps
llms-help = how to add documents, change voices, record your own voice, and fix playback
